    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 31 slate with high expectations, headlined by our three elite-tier starts. **Trea Turner** (81.27) leads the charge against Young, capitalizing on a stellar park factor and his prime leadoff position. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.79) is a must-start; while he faces a decent arm in Warren, his elite speed profile combined with a strong platoon advantage pushes him near the top of our lineup. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) rounds out this primary tier, as his power-hitting profile aligns perfectly with the park factors and favorable lineup placement. We also see high-value output from **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Junior Caminero** (74.74), both of whom benefit significantly from facing starters with inflated xERAs, providing us with a strong foundation for both power and counting stats.\n\nOur optimization process faced a difficult decision regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (58.61) and **Carson Benge** (58.97), who both landed in the \"Strong\" category but sit on the lower end of our starting spectrum. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a terrifying threat despite a tough matchup against Eovaldi; while the SP skill of his opponent dragged his score down, his elite xwOBA (0.477) makes him impossible to bench. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (45.32) is our most precarious start; facing the formidable Cease (2.94 xERA) significantly caps his efficiency, and he remains our primary candidate to be pulled if we find ourselves protecting game caps later in the week. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, and **Nelson Velazquez**, all of whom provide zero value today due to minor league assignments or rest, while internal reserves like **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** remain ready should injury or defensive adjustments necessitate a roster shakeup.",
